WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:06.178
Tokenomics Detective is about the supply side of a token: how many exist,

2
00:00:06.178 --> 00:00:10.145
how many can trade, and how that changes over time.

3
00:00:11.545 --> 00:00:14.279
There are three supply figures.

4
00:00:14.279 --> 00:00:17.189
Circulating supply can trade now.

5
00:00:17.189 --> 00:00:21.158
Total supply exists, including locked tokens.

6
00:00:21.158 --> 00:00:26.097
Maximum supply is a cap, where the protocol defines one.

7
00:00:26.097 --> 00:00:33.859
Market capitalisation uses circulating supply; fully diluted valuation uses the maximum.

8
00:00:35.259 --> 00:00:37.074
Here is a fictional token.

9
00:00:37.074 --> 00:00:39.936
Four hundred million circulate at launch.

10
00:00:39.936 --> 00:00:46.219
Two hundred million team tokens unlock after a twelve-month cliff over twenty-four months,

11
00:00:46.219 --> 00:00:52.223
and one hundred and fifty million investor tokens after a six-month cliff over twelve.

12
00:00:52.223 --> 00:00:59.274
Circulating supply grows from four hundred million to seven hundred and fifty million in three years.

13
00:01:00.674 --> 00:01:06.253
If the market value of the token stayed the same while supply nearly doubled,

14
00:01:06.253 --> 00:01:09.586
the price per token would fall by almost half.

15
00:01:09.586 --> 00:01:14.368
Supply alone can move the arithmetic, before any change in demand.

16
00:01:15.768 --> 00:01:22.749
Supply also changes through emissions, which pay participants with new tokens, and burns,

17
00:01:22.749 --> 00:01:24.397
which destroy tokens.

18
00:01:24.397 --> 00:01:27.142
Net change is issuance minus burns.

19
00:01:27.142 --> 00:01:33.418
Incentives paid in new tokens are a cost borne by every holder through dilution.

20
00:01:34.818 --> 00:01:40.992
In the course you will design vesting schedules in a three-dimensional simulator,

21
00:01:40.992 --> 00:01:46.405
test utility claims against evidence, and build a disclosure checklist.

22
00:01:46.405 --> 00:01:52.046
Unlock data in ATLAS is shown only from verified sources, never estimated.

23
00:01:52.046 --> 00:01:55.172
This is education, not investment advice.

